.TH GITHUB-COPILOT-INSTALLER 1 "September 2026" "github-copilot-installer 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
github-copilot-installer \- verified official GitHub Copilot application delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B github-copilot-installer
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installing or upgrading the helper RPM queues a one-shot systemd job after
DNF finishes. It downloads the package-selected official GitHub Copilot
AppImage, verifies its SHA-256 and identity, extracts it and creates desktop
integration. The proprietary application is not contained in the helper or
its COPR repository. Check systemctl status github-copilot-installer.service
for completion or failure. The job retries failed operations, up to three
starts in 15 minutes. Reinstalling the RPM queues another attempt.
.PP
Removing the helper RPM removes the verified application and desktop
integration. User data in ~/.copilot is preserved.
.PP
Helper versions before 0.4.0 installed GitHub's RPM instead. While that
package is installed, install and apply refuse to run; remove it with
dnf remove github.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Require root. Reconcile the release pinned in this helper package. Reject
changed or foreign files, metadata drift and downgrades. Repair missing known
desktop links from the retained verified artifact without network access.
.TP
.B update
Like install, for an existing verified installation.
.TP
.B prepare
Download and verify a stable release without root or installation.
Print schema-version-1 JSON with version, name, arch, sha256, path and source.
Retain the artifact in a private directory for the caller to inspect and remove.
.TP
.B apply
Require root. Install a prepared AppImage without network access. Requires
the exact expected SHA-256 and version. Refuses downgrades.
.TP
.B status
Show the helper, selected application version and SHA-256, and installed
application version, without network access. Unknown state is an error.
.TP
.B uninstall
Require root. Remove only verified owned application files and desktop
integration. Interrupted removal can be retried; changed or foreign files
block removal. Final RPM removal invokes this command automatically.
.TP
.B version
Print the helper version.
.TP
.B help
Print command usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-version " VERSION"
Select an explicit GitHub Copilot release instead of the packaged release.
Selects the release for install, update and prepare; required with apply.
Without this option, prepare resolves GitHub's latest stable release.
.TP
.BR \-\-assumeyes ", " \-y
Accepted for mutating commands; approval happens before the command runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-directory " DIR"
Existing destination directory for prepare. It creates a private child directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-appimage " FILE"
Regular prepared AppImage for apply. Symlinks are refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-sha256 " HEX"
Expected lowercase SHA-256 digest for apply.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/github-copilot/
AppImage, extracted application, launcher, desktop entry and receipt.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/github
Application launch command.
.TP
.B /usr/local/share/applications/github-copilot.desktop
Desktop integration, including GitHub Copilot sign-in links.
.TP
.I ~/.copilot
Upstream application data. This helper never removes or modifies it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo github-copilot-installer install
github-copilot-installer status
sudo github-copilot-installer update
sudo github-copilot-installer uninstall
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The upstream AppImage is unsigned. Installation therefore requires the SHA-256
digest pinned in this package or published by the official GitHub release API,
and an exact official release URL. Redirects are restricted to HTTPS on the
official GitHub API, repository release path and GitHub release asset host.
Only published stable releases are accepted. Preparation JSON is information
for the caller, not authorization to install.
